When to Choose Each 

• Choose JavaScript for: Small projects, rapid prototyping, or when you need a fast development cycle without the overhead of a build step. 
• Choose TypeScript for: Large-scale applications, projects with multiple developers, and software where long-term maintainability and fewer production bugs are critical. [1, 3, 4, 14]  

